{"name":"Musical Mist","hex":"#f8eae6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"musical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, belonging or relating to music, or to its performance or notation.","Pleasing to the ear; sounding agreeably; having the qualities of music; melodious; harmonious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stage performance, show or film that involves singing, dancing and musical numbers performed by the cast as well as acting.","A meeting or a party for a musical entertainment; a musicale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musical"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist","wikidata":"Q192196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg/500px-Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg?u